WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:11.179
[ Watch on KissFlix.co ]

2
00:11.449 --> 00:12.784
Okay.

3
00:12.867 --> 00:15.245
One, two…

4
00:17.080 --> 00:20.625
When I was young, my family was your typical middle-class family.

5
00:20.708 --> 00:21.668
Say bye.

6
00:21.751 --> 00:22.585
Oh!

7
00:24.212 --> 00:25.088
Mm.

8
00:25.755 --> 00:26.714
But…

9
00:26.798 --> 00:28.049
NOTICE OF SEIZURE

10
00:28.133 --> 00:29.134
Move, please.

11
00:29.217 --> 00:32.428
…that typical family went bankrupt after cosigning a loan.

12
00:32.512 --> 00:33.680
My dad was devastated,

13
00:33.763 --> 00:36.599
and no matter how much he paid off, the debt stayed the same.

14
00:37.350 --> 00:40.687
One day, he told us he found a good job, and disappeared.

15
00:40.770 --> 00:41.729
MOM, HYEOK-JUN, JI-YOON

16
00:41.813 --> 00:45.984
The three of us who were left kept moving from one single-room apartment to another.

17
00:49.195 --> 00:51.114
Every night when I couldn't sleep,

18
00:51.739 --> 00:55.577
all I could think about was the TV show that my family went on together.

19
00:55.660 --> 00:57.412
It was called, A Father's Miracle.

20
00:57.495 --> 01:01.124
The family is coming in. Let's give them a big round of applause!

21
01:01.624 --> 01:05.086
Now that practice is over, family, what do you think? Will your father…

22
01:05.170 --> 01:06.254
Although…

23
01:06.337 --> 01:07.505
What about you?

24
01:07.589 --> 01:09.299
…it wasn't exactly a good memory.

25
01:09.382 --> 01:11.634
Yeah. No one tries harder than my father does.

26
01:11.718 --> 01:13.303
- I hope he wins! - Ah!

27
01:13.386 --> 01:16.431
Now, today's challenge for A Father's Miracle is…

28
01:16.514 --> 01:19.225
Juggling for ten seconds while riding a unicycle.

29
01:19.309 --> 01:22.020
Will the father succeed in performing this miracle?

30
01:22.103 --> 01:25.899
Okay, the father has mounted the unicycle.

31
01:26.566 --> 01:28.610
Oh, this is tense. Can he do it?

32
01:30.737 --> 01:32.238
Oh!

33
01:32.322 --> 01:33.907
Okay, he's let go.

34
01:33.990 --> 01:37.577
- He's trying for balance. Now juggling. - Yes. Keep going!

35
01:37.660 --> 01:39.662
Here he goes, and… Oh no!

36
01:41.080 --> 01:43.625
- No, he fell! Uh, sir! - Oh my gosh.

37
01:43.708 --> 01:46.169
Unfortunately, today's miracle has failed.

38
01:46.252 --> 01:48.338
- And from then on… - Oh no!

39
01:48.421 --> 01:51.674
…my dad searched for jobs that were an easy payday.

40
02:08.441 --> 02:09.567
Sometimes I wonder,

41
02:10.693 --> 02:12.946
if I hadn't sent in the application…

42
02:15.323 --> 02:16.699
would things be different?

43
03:13.965 --> 03:17.176
DEAD-END JOB

44
03:18.386 --> 03:21.347
THE WALLS DON'T TALK

45
03:23.641 --> 03:28.771
You know you're not the only temp worker at Spider Staffing Agency, don't you?

46
03:29.314 --> 03:32.066
I bet you could never find a gig as easy as that.

47
03:35.111 --> 03:36.446
The work I do,

48
03:37.739 --> 03:39.657
it's a really easy gig.

49
03:52.587 --> 03:56.674
LOOK RIGHT IF YOU'RE NOT BUSY

50
03:56.758 --> 03:58.009
Oh shit!

51
03:59.510 --> 04:01.054
No, no, no.

52
04:01.804 --> 04:03.681
I thought you might be here.

53
04:04.557 --> 04:07.268
How… How… How could you… What… What are you doing here?

54
04:07.352 --> 04:09.604
I was just out for a walk and saw you.

55
04:09.687 --> 04:11.647
You were just out walking?

56
04:11.731 --> 04:13.149
Yeah.

57
04:15.068 --> 04:16.819
I thought you might have run away.

58
04:19.906 --> 04:22.658
I've met quite a few temps in my time.

59
04:24.118 --> 04:26.371
This job can be kind of

60
04:27.455 --> 04:30.666
overwhelming to most people, and they can back down sometimes.

61
04:30.750 --> 04:32.418
They're not as strong as you are.

62
04:32.502 --> 04:34.921
After one or two times, they either give up or disappear.

63
04:35.004 --> 04:37.548
What do you mean by "disappear?" Do they come back?

64
04:39.717 --> 04:42.220
You're a natural at temp jobs.

65
04:43.262 --> 04:46.140
Yangcheon Bio Clinic, what did you do there?

66
04:46.641 --> 04:48.559
Huh? Uh…

67
04:49.560 --> 04:52.355
And how did you get out of the milk delivery?

68
04:54.649 --> 04:56.526
It's almost as if you had help.

69
04:57.777 --> 05:00.655
Uh, uh, well, there's just the penalty fee.

70
05:00.738 --> 05:02.657
Oh! That's what you want!

71
05:04.909 --> 05:07.954
The penalty must be paid if I tell anyone about my jobs.

72
05:09.539 --> 05:10.998
That's what you're doing here?

73
05:12.625 --> 05:15.294
Actually, no. I am interested in you.

74
05:16.254 --> 05:19.048
You made an unauthorized departure during the milk delivery,

75
05:19.132 --> 05:22.927
and then the Bio Clinic job you did after,

76
05:23.428 --> 05:24.679
you did for nothing.

77
05:25.179 --> 05:28.015
I can't let a talent like you walk away.

78
05:30.309 --> 05:31.519
Sir,

79
05:32.353 --> 05:33.938
can I ask you something?

80
05:35.940 --> 05:37.024
Sure.

81
05:37.733 --> 05:40.736
Do you know, uh, uh, uh… Byeon Min…

82
05:40.820 --> 05:42.655
Someone named Byeon Min-su?

83
05:44.323 --> 05:45.324
Do you?

84
05:48.619 --> 05:49.787
Byeon Min-su?

85
05:52.081 --> 05:53.708
Byeon Min-su…

86
05:55.418 --> 05:57.670
Byeon Min-su.

87
05:58.588 --> 06:00.298
Byeon Min-su…

88
06:05.887 --> 06:07.263
I don't believe I do.

89
06:08.473 --> 06:09.515
Ah, uh…

90
06:11.267 --> 06:12.268
There.

91
06:12.351 --> 06:16.731
CONSTRUCTION SITE, DAY-NIGHT SHIFT 1,600 TIMES THE DAILY WAGE, 2 P.M.-10 P.M.

92
06:16.814 --> 06:18.649
Now, let's see what you can do.

93
06:19.692 --> 06:22.570
- See you soon. - I'm not gonna do any more.

94
06:22.653 --> 06:23.905
Just think it over.

95
06:23.988 --> 06:25.781
You don't have to decide today.

96
06:27.408 --> 06:29.035
Hm. What do you say to that?

97
06:29.827 --> 06:30.912
You need the money.

98
06:38.294 --> 06:39.295
FIRE HOT TTEOKBOKKI

99
06:39.378 --> 06:41.547
Quite the storm system is heading our way.

100
06:42.423 --> 06:44.217
We'll tell you when to take out the umbrellas.

101
06:44.300 --> 06:47.595
And later, statement necklaces are back and bigger than ever.

102
06:47.678 --> 06:51.307
So… what brings you two here today?

103
06:51.390 --> 06:53.184
Well, because Hyeok-jun wanted to.

104
06:53.684 --> 06:55.269
- Oh yeah? - Mm-hmm.

105
06:55.353 --> 06:57.355
You could have told him to just video call me.

106
06:57.438 --> 06:59.565
I think he was just too shy.

107
06:59.649 --> 07:02.610
Mom, pretend you don't know and be nice.

108
07:03.861 --> 07:05.279
About what?

109
07:07.323 --> 07:08.407
Oh…

110
07:08.491 --> 07:12.119
I knew it. I had a feeling the interview wouldn't go well.

111
07:12.787 --> 07:14.288
Wait, what?

112
07:16.582 --> 07:20.461
- He had an interview too? - Oh, that's right. How did yours go?

113
08:18.394 --> 08:20.104
"Money to pay back?"

114
08:20.187 --> 08:22.315
UNCLE CHEOL-I 150,000 BY MID APR SANG-WOO 190,000 BY APR

115
08:22.398 --> 08:24.442
SANG-MIN 180,000 BY EARLY AUG MI-GYEONG 320,000 BY DEC

116
08:38.623 --> 08:41.751
"Tunnel construction. Fifty times…"

117
08:42.335 --> 08:44.837
"Quarry. One hundred times."

118
08:45.338 --> 08:47.882
"Construction site, 200 times?"

119
08:49.008 --> 08:50.134
The last…

120
08:51.052 --> 08:52.178
The last.

121
09:00.686 --> 09:03.272
"Construction site, night shift."

122
09:03.773 --> 09:05.441
1,600 TIMES THE DAILY WAGE, 2 P.M.-10 P.M.

123
09:05.524 --> 09:08.319
"Construction site, day-night shift."

124
09:33.969 --> 09:37.890
ACCEPT

125
09:50.861 --> 09:52.697
BYEON JI-YOON DID YOU TAKE ANOTHER PART-TIMEJOB?

126
09:52.780 --> 09:54.240
GET YOUR ASS BACK HOME BEFORE I KILL…

127
09:54.323 --> 09:55.533
MISSED CALL BYEON JI-YOON

128
10:07.086 --> 10:08.462
You Byeon Hyeok-jun?

129
10:10.423 --> 10:12.133
Uh, yeah, that's me.

130
10:12.216 --> 10:14.301
You're a young guy. Hop on in.

131
10:18.305 --> 10:19.557
What? Get in.

132
10:20.766 --> 10:21.726
Okay.

133
10:50.546 --> 10:52.047
All right, here we go.

134
10:52.548 --> 10:53.674
You ready?

135
10:54.467 --> 10:56.635
Come on, move it. Let's go!

136
10:59.805 --> 11:01.724
God, my back.

137
11:03.350 --> 11:07.313
- What're you doing? Get over here. - I hope we finish before dark.

138
11:09.023 --> 11:12.151
Today's all about cleanup. We're just clearing the place. Got it?

139
11:12.234 --> 11:14.487
- Yes, cleanup! - Cleanup!

140
11:14.570 --> 11:15.946
Everyone, stay focused.

141
11:16.447 --> 11:20.075
CONSTRUCTION SITE, DAY-NIGHT SHIFT 1,600 TIMES THE DAILY WAGE

142
11:20.159 --> 11:22.411
STARTS AT 2 P.M. ENDS AT 10 P.M.

143
11:22.495 --> 11:24.622
We'll start with the supports. Remove them quickly.

144
11:24.705 --> 11:25.873
Yes, sir!

145
11:26.373 --> 11:28.125
Hey, over here. Move it over here.

146
11:28.209 --> 11:31.462
- You can tell he's a rookie. - We don't have much time!

147
11:31.545 --> 11:34.131
- Come on, move, move! - Hurry it up! Faster!

148
11:36.801 --> 11:39.345
- Hey, what's that noise? - Oh God.

149
11:39.428 --> 11:41.972
Everyone, get over here! Now, damn it!

150
11:42.556 --> 11:44.308
- What the hell is this? - Whoa, whoa!

151
11:44.391 --> 11:48.270
Why are you pulling down these supports? We just installed them yesterday!

152
11:48.354 --> 11:49.688
Are you insane?

153
11:51.565 --> 11:53.901
What're you doing? The only thing we speak here is English!

154
11:53.984 --> 11:57.822
English? Come on! What, big man? You'll be nice if I speak English?

155
11:57.905 --> 11:59.490
Hey, asshole, get back right now!

156
11:59.573 --> 12:01.659
Who ordered you guys to do this?

157
12:02.326 --> 12:05.204
We're taking down the supports! Hey, keep going!

158
12:05.287 --> 12:09.166
Jackass! Are you taking responsibility when the lack of supports hurts someone?

159
12:09.792 --> 12:11.377
Oh! Stop it. No!

160
12:12.837 --> 12:14.296
Grab 'em! Grab the bastards!

161
12:14.380 --> 12:16.257
Yeah, you heard. Don't come any closer!

162
12:18.634 --> 12:19.718
You piece of shit!

163
12:19.802 --> 12:23.138
Foreman, sir! Foreman, sir! Stop, stop, stop it, stop!

164
12:28.519 --> 12:31.981
- Whoa! Sir, no! You're gonna kill him! - Let go!

165
12:37.319 --> 12:38.445
You son of a--

166
12:59.174 --> 13:00.217
Calm down!

167
13:01.468 --> 13:04.346
We should stop working now. Get up. We can't stay.

168
13:04.847 --> 13:06.557
Was that an earthquake?

169
13:06.640 --> 13:09.101
Damn morons. Hey!

170
13:09.184 --> 13:12.146
- Come on! - Go! Go. Everyone, okay?

171
13:12.646 --> 13:14.815
I don't even know what happened, but we gotta go.

172
13:20.195 --> 13:22.239
Beware of your foreman.

173
13:26.785 --> 13:29.246
Now we have to take down the banner outside.

174
13:29.330 --> 13:30.664
You want us to do that too?

175
13:30.748 --> 13:32.333
The scaffolding's too weak

176
13:33.125 --> 13:36.295
Since when has proper scaffolding helped us in the past?

177
13:37.004 --> 13:39.965
Come on, Kim. You take that side, okay?

178
13:40.049 --> 13:42.217
Oh, crap, why are we doing the banner?

179
13:42.301 --> 13:43.177
Hey, newbie?

180
13:44.261 --> 13:45.095
Yeah?

181
13:45.596 --> 13:47.473
You ever play on the jungle gym as a kid?

182
13:48.307 --> 13:49.141
What?

183
13:50.392 --> 13:52.728
Yep. Just like a jungle gym.

184
13:54.855 --> 13:56.106
Oh!

185
13:57.650 --> 13:58.734
Oh, shi…

186
14:00.527 --> 14:02.446
Don't be scared. That's why there's safety hooks.

187
14:09.328 --> 14:12.039
You've got to latch the safety hook on the outside.

188
14:12.706 --> 14:14.625
That's it, that's it.

189
14:20.255 --> 14:21.632
Oh, sh…

190
14:42.945 --> 14:44.697
That's it. Now cut it.

191
14:57.543 --> 15:00.337
"The price of thirty lives buried…

192
15:02.715 --> 15:04.591
will be repaid with death."

193
15:08.053 --> 15:09.722
Oh!

194
15:17.646 --> 15:21.692
No! Damn it! What are you doing? Get down there now!

195
15:22.192 --> 15:23.986
Hurry up! Run! Go!

196
15:24.903 --> 15:26.280
Son of a bi…

197
15:26.905 --> 15:29.992
Kim? Brother? Hang in there, okay. There's an ambulance on the way, huh?

198
15:30.075 --> 15:31.660
They're almost here.

199
15:31.744 --> 15:33.495
Just hang in there.

200
15:33.579 --> 15:35.497
- What are they doing? - What is it?

201
15:35.581 --> 15:37.666
That bastard just told them to go.

202
15:38.542 --> 15:40.085
Hey! Over here!

203
15:41.295 --> 15:42.671
You made them go? What the hell?!

204
15:43.255 --> 15:45.257
What the fuck are you doing? Get them back!

205
15:47.217 --> 15:49.178
- Who do you think you are? - What's the problem?

206
15:49.261 --> 15:51.555
This piece of shit made the ambulance leave!

207
15:53.223 --> 15:54.725
Can't you see he's hurt?

208
15:54.808 --> 15:56.268
Are you crazy?

209
15:57.686 --> 16:00.647
I was told not to let the ambulance in.

210
16:01.190 --> 16:02.816
You transport anyone who gets hurt.

211
16:02.900 --> 16:06.111
What's with this guy? Must be a Koryoin?

212
16:06.195 --> 16:07.446
Get back to work.

213
16:07.529 --> 16:10.449
Hey, asshole! Listen to me, all right. Look!

214
16:10.532 --> 16:13.660
A man's going to die. He's bleeding out!

215
16:13.744 --> 16:17.706
Come on. Don't pretend like you don't fucking know!

216
16:17.790 --> 16:19.917
You knew all along, didn't you?

217
16:20.000 --> 16:23.462
I know you did. Are you saying you didn't? But you did know.

218
16:23.545 --> 16:25.255
Whoa! Stop. Stop it.

219
16:26.882 --> 16:28.092
Just cool down.

220
16:28.175 --> 16:30.511
How can we fucking work like this?

221
16:35.224 --> 16:36.183
Like what?

222
16:36.266 --> 16:38.393
You sent the ambulance away back there.

223
16:38.936 --> 16:40.395
What, are you trying to kill us?

224
16:41.730 --> 16:42.981
Did I send it away?

225
16:43.774 --> 16:45.359
What does it matter to you, huh?

226
16:45.442 --> 16:48.278
This isn't what you fucking promised us, dude!

227
16:48.862 --> 16:50.989
What promise? Hey!

228
16:51.490 --> 16:54.451
You thought it wouldn't be dangerous. Is that it?

229
16:55.119 --> 16:55.994
Huh?

230
16:56.870 --> 16:59.706
Fucking hell. This is bullshit.

231
17:00.207 --> 17:01.667
That's not what he meant!

232
17:02.793 --> 17:05.337
That might work on the other guys, but it won't work on us,

233
17:05.420 --> 17:06.755
you goddamn selfish prick.

234
17:07.381 --> 17:08.841
We don't plan on dying here,

235
17:08.924 --> 17:11.552
so go find another crew to do your dirty work.

236
17:11.635 --> 17:13.262
Let's get the van and load up!

237
17:13.971 --> 17:15.889
- Hey. - Y… Yeah?

238
17:16.515 --> 17:17.599
You leaving?

239
17:18.433 --> 17:21.103
Oh, no, no, no. I have to… I have to stay.

240
17:22.604 --> 17:25.482
- So be it. - Hey!

241
17:27.192 --> 17:30.237
You'll never work again. I promise you that much!

242
17:32.698 --> 17:34.158
Rookie, you're staying until the end?

243
17:35.993 --> 17:37.536
Uh, um, yes, sir.

244
17:38.036 --> 17:41.331
Good. We'll manage without those bastards.

245
17:45.961 --> 17:47.212
Ah, sh…

246
17:48.213 --> 17:49.214
Hurry up.

247
17:58.807 --> 18:00.475
Put that down and take a break.

248
18:00.559 --> 18:01.476
Okay.

249
18:13.071 --> 18:14.448
I was wondering,

250
18:15.032 --> 18:17.743
is it… is it always so dangerous?

251
18:17.826 --> 18:19.536
You think buildings just happen?

252
18:20.370 --> 18:22.748
They happen by grinding people into them.

253
18:26.335 --> 18:27.586
Especially here.

254
18:28.212 --> 18:29.630
Grinding people…

255
18:35.052 --> 18:38.555
You interested in this kind of work? You wanna join our team?

256
18:39.056 --> 18:41.183
From what I can see, you don't have a head for this job.

257
18:41.266 --> 18:42.893
But you're desperate. Good enough.

258
18:43.435 --> 18:46.521
Oh, th… that's nice. I appreciate it. It's just…

259
18:46.605 --> 18:49.149
Listen. I'm telling ya, anybody can do it.

260
18:51.693 --> 18:52.653
Yeah…

261
18:52.736 --> 18:54.613
Even people who aren't in good shape.

262
18:55.530 --> 18:57.616
We had this one guy. Name was Byeon.

263
19:00.619 --> 19:03.121
B… Wait, "Byeon," you said?

264
19:04.456 --> 19:05.791
Horrible shape, that guy.

265
19:05.874 --> 19:08.210
But no matter how much I cursed at him, he was persistent.

266
19:08.919 --> 19:10.754
A bit of a pest, between us.

267
19:11.755 --> 19:13.507
Then something bad happened to him.

268
19:15.133 --> 19:19.429
So, um, this person, Byeon, you're taking about, did he

269
19:20.889 --> 19:22.641
have all ten of his fingers left?

270
19:24.101 --> 19:25.227
Did he?

271
19:26.812 --> 19:29.231
I think maybe he had a few fingers missing.

272
19:35.779 --> 19:37.656
Or else he'd be better at his job.

273
19:41.076 --> 19:43.328
All right, let's move to the basement.

274
19:43.412 --> 19:44.538
We're almost done.

275
19:45.080 --> 19:48.417
You and I both need to make money so we can go back to our families.

276
19:52.546 --> 19:53.714
Follow me.

277
20:01.596 --> 20:03.181
Watch your step.

278
20:03.265 --> 20:04.266
Okay.

279
20:10.147 --> 20:11.273
Turn that off!

280
20:15.610 --> 20:17.738
The dust in the basement is a fire hazard.

281
20:18.405 --> 20:19.698
That light could spark.

282
20:20.198 --> 20:21.283
Okay.

283
20:35.130 --> 20:38.842
Okay, you put that over there. I'll stack these inside.

284
20:39.343 --> 20:41.011
Okay.

285
21:09.706 --> 21:10.624
Let's stop.

286
21:12.000 --> 21:14.169
Uh… Y… Yeah. Uh, okay.

287
21:14.753 --> 21:16.129
All right, good work.

288
21:16.213 --> 21:18.715
Looks like it's about time. Let's go.

289
21:19.633 --> 21:22.010
Oh, um, so…

290
22:37.544 --> 22:39.629
Oh! Oh!

291
22:51.725 --> 22:52.934
Curious, huh?

292
22:56.938 --> 22:59.441
Why we're doing work that doesn't make sense.

293
23:05.947 --> 23:07.782
Accidents are necessary.

294
23:08.450 --> 23:10.744
This building, it needs to feed on people.

295
23:13.038 --> 23:15.790
A shaman said, when they were picking the site for the building,

296
23:15.874 --> 23:17.918
to build a bone tower.

297
23:19.753 --> 23:22.964
One hundred bodies as a sacrifice for riches.

298
23:23.048 --> 23:26.468
For wealth that lasts generations. I don't want to do this either.

299
23:27.344 --> 23:30.847
But if I handle this, the real money will flow.

300
23:32.474 --> 23:34.226
Isn't that why you're here?

301
23:36.394 --> 23:37.270
And besides,

302
23:38.188 --> 23:39.481
we're alive, right?

303
23:39.981 --> 23:41.525
We got money in our hands.

304
23:41.608 --> 23:42.943
And we're innocent.

305
23:44.694 --> 23:45.779
You know?

306
24:21.773 --> 24:26.027
The dead ones are the idiots, damn it. Is making a living a crime?

307
24:27.362 --> 24:28.405
Huh?

308
24:29.030 --> 24:30.949
Is survival a crime?

309
24:50.844 --> 24:53.722
Stop, stop, stop, stop, stop, stop!

310
25:04.441 --> 25:06.860
Did you do that to all the people who worked here?

311
25:06.943 --> 25:09.195
- I didn't! - To all the people who were like Byeon?

312
25:09.988 --> 25:11.531
Was that the thing you did to everyone?!

313
25:11.615 --> 25:12.741
I don't know!

314
25:13.241 --> 25:14.367
I can't say.

315
25:14.451 --> 25:15.827
What was his full name?

316
25:16.536 --> 25:18.622
- Mr. Byeon? - I don't remember.

317
25:18.705 --> 25:21.374
- We only called him Byeon. - You don't remember?

318
25:22.375 --> 25:24.961
After all of that, you can't even remember his name!

319
25:25.045 --> 25:26.379
- Huh?! - Byeon Min-su!

320
25:29.716 --> 25:30.800
Min-su.

321
25:30.884 --> 25:32.218
Byeon Min-su.

322
25:39.017 --> 25:40.018
You killed him?

323
25:41.311 --> 25:42.520
No, no.

324
25:43.480 --> 25:44.773
Don't you lie to me!

325
25:44.856 --> 25:48.109
I'm not! No, Byeon isn't buried there. I know he wasn't.

326
25:49.319 --> 25:50.945
But… But… But… But what?

327
25:51.446 --> 25:52.405
He isn't dead.

328
25:52.906 --> 25:54.282
He vanished.

329
25:54.908 --> 25:55.867
Like that.

330
25:56.910 --> 25:57.994
Where did he go?

331
25:59.704 --> 26:01.456
I said, where did he go?!

332
26:01.539 --> 26:02.999
I don't know!

333
26:05.794 --> 26:07.003
I swear to you.

334
26:09.047 --> 26:10.674
He passed through a door,

335
26:11.675 --> 26:13.176
and never returned.

336
26:17.889 --> 26:20.850
He must be around somewhere.

337
27:03.435 --> 27:10.442
YOUR FAMILY IS PRAYING FOR YOUR SAFETY AGAIN TODAY

338
27:10.525 --> 27:16.698
♪ The sewing machine Spins so well, it goes on spinning ♪

339
27:19.367 --> 27:25.874
♪ Red flowers, yellow flowers Even when the garden is in full bloom ♪

340
27:27.834 --> 27:34.340
♪ White butterflies, flower butterflies Even when they flutter over the wall ♪
